  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "He was a compost.",
   "texto": [
    "To tell what you did, the **passé composé** is used. It is formed with the present of **avoir** + the **participio**: **J'ai mangé** (I ate, I ate).",
    "The partition of the verbs in -er ends in **-é**: manger → **mangé**, regarder → **regardé**, travailler → **travaillé**. Sounds just like the infinitive.",
    "In Spanish we distinguish «I ate.» and «I've eaten.»; when speaking French, the common passé serves both."
   ]
  },
